{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files / storage APIs"}]},{"type":"text","value":" let you upload a media asset once and reference it later by a lightweight handle, instead of re-sending base64 (or relying on the provider to re-fetch a public URL) on every request. That means large or reused inputs are uploaded a single time — lower latency and bandwidth, no re-buffering of base64 on memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers) — plus access to provider-side file lifecycle (TTL, deletion)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack AI exposes this as a tree-shakeable "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"files"},{"type":"text","value":" adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" per provider, paired with a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'file' }"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"./multimodal-content.md#file-handle-files-api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"content source"}]},{"type":"text","value":" you drop into a message."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"files-adapters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Files adapters"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each provider with a native surface has a factory: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropicFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"geminiFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":". They read the same API-key env var as the provider's other adapters. To pass a key explicitly, use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"create*Files(apiKey)"},{"type":"text","value":" variants ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createOpenaiFiles"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAnthropicFiles"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGeminiFiles"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createGrokFiles"},{"type":"text","value":"). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falFiles(config)"},{"type":"text","value":" takes its key in the config object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createOpenaiFiles, openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { geminiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\nimport { anthropicFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { falFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles() // reads OPENAI_API_KEY\nconst filesWithKey = createOpenaiFiles('sk-your-key') // explicit key","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"uploadfile","children":[{"type":"text","value":"uploadFile"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Drive an adapter with the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uploadFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" activity function. It accepts a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Blob"},{"type":"text","value":" (memory-efficient — preferred for large assets) or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ data, mimeType }"},{"type":"text","value":" where "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" is base64, and returns a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FileHandle"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: openaiFiles(),\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n// handle: { id, provider, uri?, mimeType?, sizeBytes?, expiresAt?, filename? }","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":" — the provider handle used for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":" (OpenAI/Anthropic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":", Gemini file resource name, fal storage URL)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"uri"},{"type":"text","value":": the handle's URL form when the provider exposes one (Gemini file URI, fal storage URL, Grok public URL). It is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"undefined"},{"type":"text","value":" for OpenAI and Anthropic, whose handles are opaque ids."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expiresAt"},{"type":"text","value":" — epoch milliseconds, when the provider schedules the handle to expire."}]}]}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime note (Gemini upload)."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"geminiFiles().upload()"},{"type":"text","value":" uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@google/genai"},{"type":"text","value":"'s\nresumable upload, which sets an explicit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Content-Length"},{"type":"text","value":" header on a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Blob"},{"type":"text","value":"-body\nrequest. Some server runtimes reject that with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch failed"},{"type":"text","value":" /\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"InvalidArgumentError: invalid content-length header"},{"type":"text","value":". On "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Start / Nitro"}]},{"type":"text","value":"\nthis fails on older Nitro (observed on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nitro@3.0.1-alpha.2"},{"type":"text","value":") and works on current\nNitro (verified on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"nitro@3.0.260610-beta"},{"type":"text","value":") — upgrade Nitro if you hit it. Native\nNode (and the production "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"node-server"},{"type":"text","value":" build) are unaffected. OpenAI, Anthropic, and\nfal uploads use different transports and don't exercise this path."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"getfile-and-deletefile","children":[{"type":"text","value":"getFile and deleteFile"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers with a lifecycle API support "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deleteFile()"},{"type":"text","value":". Both accept the handle itself (preferred — the handle's provider type rejects a foreign provider's handle at compile time) or its raw "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"id"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { deleteFile, getFile, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: files,\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n\nconst meta = await getFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })\nawait deleteFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal storage is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"upload-only"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":" defines no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":", and calling "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deleteFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" with it throws a clear error."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"grok-xai-handles-are-public-urls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok (xAI): handles are public URLs"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokFiles()"},{"type":"text","value":" uploads to the xAI Files API, then mints a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.x.ai/developers/files/public-urls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"public URL"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the stored object and uses that URL as the handle's reference."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"xAI takes a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":" only on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_file"},{"type":"text","value":" (documents), and only on agentic-capable models. Its image path takes a URL. A public URL works for both, so one handle covers every modality on every chat model."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\nimport { pngBase64 } from './image-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  // Omit `expiresAfter` for a URL that does not expire.\n  adapter: grokFiles({ expiresAfter: 86_400 }),\n  input: { data: pngBase64, mimeType: 'image/png' },\n})\n// handle.id  -> 'file_abc123'            (lifecycle)\n// handle.uri -> 'https://files-cdn.x.ai/…' (wire reference)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"xAI limits to know:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"50 MiB per file, and PNG, JPEG, MP4, or PDF only."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"expiresAfter"},{"type":"text","value":" runs from 3600 seconds (one hour) to 2592000 (thirty days)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Up to 1000 active public URLs per team."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minting is idempotent, so re-uploading the same file returns the same URL."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To stop a URL resolving without deleting the file, call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"revokePublicUrl(handle.id)"},{"type":"text","value":" on the adapter. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deleteFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" removes the file itself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" mints the public URL to put it on the handle. After you revoke a URL, do not call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFile()"},{"type":"text","value":" for that file, or the file gets a public URL again."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"referencing-a-handle-in-a-message","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Referencing a handle in a message"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSourceFromHandle(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" to turn a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"FileHandle"},{"type":"text","value":" into a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'file' }"},{"type":"text","value":" content source:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import type { ContentPartFileSource } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst source: ContentPartFileSource = {\n  type: 'file',\n  value: 'file-abc',\n  provider: 'openai',\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" is the handle exactly as the provider issued it. Treat it as opaque."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" names the adapter that issued it."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each adapter maps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":" to its native wire field: OpenAI and Anthropic "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":", Gemini "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileData.fileUri"},{"type":"text","value":", fal storage URL, Grok public URL."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A handle only works with the provider that issued it. If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provider"},{"type":"text","value":" names a different adapter, that adapter throws a clear error. Adapters that cannot consume file handles at all are rejected before any mapping starts."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"server-upload-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server: upload + reference"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, fileSourceFromHandle, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicFiles, anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nexport async function askAboutPdf(pdfBase64: string, request: string) {\n  // Upload once; reuse the handle across turns.\n  const handle = await uploadFile({\n    adapter: anthropicFiles(),\n    input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n  })\n\n  return chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-5'),\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          { type: 'text', content: request },\n          { type: 'document', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"client-reuse-a-handle-across-requests","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client: reuse a handle across requests"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Upload needs the provider key, so it happens on the server. The browser keeps the handle it gets back and puts it in the message on each turn."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Store the handle the upload endpoint returned. Keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ id, provider, uri, mimeType }"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build the source with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSourceFromHandle(handle)"},{"type":"text","value":" and put it in the message content."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the server, pass the messages to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" as usual."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the browser, import "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileSourceFromHandle"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai/client"},{"type":"text","value":". That entry does not load server code:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { fileSourceFromHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\nimport type { FileHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\n\n// `handle` came from your upload endpoint and is stored client-side.\nfunction AskAboutFile({ handle }: { handle: FileHandle }) {\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() =>\n        sendMessage({\n          content: [\n            { type: 'text', content: 'Describe this' },\n            { type: 'image', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n          ],\n        })\n      }\n      type=\"button\"\n    >\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On the server, the file part arrives in the messages. Use a text adapter from the provider that issued the handle:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nexport function runTurn(messages: Array<ModelMessage>) {\n  return chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'), messages })\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A handle from another provider throws before any request. For example, an OpenAI handle sent to a Gemini adapter fails in preflight. It is never dropped and never sent as a URL."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"provider-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider support"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handle referenced as"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiFiles()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Responses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_image"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_file"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Anthropic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropicFiles()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":" message source (sends the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"files-api-2025-04-14"},{"type":"text","value":" beta)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"geminiFiles()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fileData.fileUri"},{"type":"text","value":" (the handle URI)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falFiles()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"storage URL (used like any URL)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"upload-only"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grok (xAI)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grokFiles()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"public URL (used like any URL)"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Gemini and fal handles are URLs, so they also round-trip through a plain "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'url' }"},{"type":"text","value":" source; OpenAI and Anthropic handles are opaque ids that require the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'file' }"},{"type":"text","value":" source."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"providers-and-endpoints-that-can-t-consume-references","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers and endpoints that can't consume references"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapters that can consume file references declare a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"supportsFileSources"},{"type":"text","value":" capability; for everyone else (Groq, Bedrock, Mistral, OpenRouter, Ollama, BytePlus, Cohere, and any adapter written before this feature existed) "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"embed()"},{"type":"text","value":" reject "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ type: 'file' }"},{"type":"text","value":" sources "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"before any request is built"}]},{"type":"text","value":", so a reference can never be silently mis-mapped onto a URL or data field."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Some endpoints on supporting providers also have no \"reference an uploaded handle\" option — OpenAI's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"images/edits"},{"type":"text","value":" and Sora "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"input_reference"},{"type":"text","value":", and Gemini's Veo, need the actual bytes (or, for Veo, a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"gs://"},{"type":"text","value":" URI). The OpenAI "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat Completions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" image path also references images only by URL/data URI, not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":" — use the Responses adapter ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":") for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"file_id"},{"type":"text","value":" images. These throw a clear endpoint-specific error."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"files-adapters","text":"Files adapters","level":2},{"id":"uploadfile","text":"uploadFile","level":3},{"id":"getfile-and-deletefile","text":"getFile and deleteFile","level":3},{"id":"grok-xai-handles-are-public-urls","text":"Grok (xAI): handles are public URLs","level":3},{"id":"referencing-a-handle-in-a-message","text":"Referencing a handle in a message","level":2},{"id":"server-upload-reference","text":"Server: upload + reference","level":3},{"id":"client-reuse-a-handle-across-requests","text":"Client: reuse a handle across requests","level":3},{"id":"provider-support","text":"Provider support","level":2},{"id":"providers-and-endpoints-that-can-t-consume-references","text":"Providers and endpoints that can't consume references","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nProvider **Files / storage APIs** let you upload a media asset once and reference it later by a lightweight handle, instead of re-sending base64 (or relying on the provider to re-fetch a public URL) on every request. That means large or reused inputs are uploaded a single time — lower latency and bandwidth, no re-buffering of base64 on memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers) — plus access to provider-side file lifecycle (TTL, deletion).\n\nTanStack AI exposes this as a tree-shakeable **`files` adapter** per provider, paired with a `{ type: 'file' }` [content source](./multimodal-content.md#file-handle-files-api) you drop into a message.\n\n## Files adapters\n\nEach provider with a native surface has a factory: `openaiFiles()`, `anthropicFiles()`, `geminiFiles()`, `grokFiles()`, and `falFiles()`. They read the same API-key env var as the provider's other adapters. To pass a key explicitly, use the `create*Files(apiKey)` variants (`createOpenaiFiles`, `createAnthropicFiles`, `createGeminiFiles`, `createGrokFiles`). `falFiles(config)` takes its key in the config object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiFiles, openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { geminiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\nimport { anthropicFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { falFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles() // reads OPENAI_API_KEY\nconst filesWithKey = createOpenaiFiles('sk-your-key') // explicit key\n```\n\n### uploadFile\n\nDrive an adapter with the `uploadFile()` activity function. It accepts a `Blob` (memory-efficient — preferred for large assets) or `{ data, mimeType }` where `data` is base64, and returns a `FileHandle`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: openaiFiles(),\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n// handle: { id, provider, uri?, mimeType?, sizeBytes?, expiresAt?, filename? }\n```\n\n- `id` — the provider handle used for `get` / `delete` (OpenAI/Anthropic `file_id`, Gemini file resource name, fal storage URL).\n- `uri`: the handle's URL form when the provider exposes one (Gemini file URI, fal storage URL, Grok public URL). It is `undefined` for OpenAI and Anthropic, whose handles are opaque ids.\n- `expiresAt` — epoch milliseconds, when the provider schedules the handle to expire.\n\n> **Runtime note (Gemini upload).** `geminiFiles().upload()` uses `@google/genai`'s\n> resumable upload, which sets an explicit `Content-Length` header on a `Blob`-body\n> request. Some server runtimes reject that with `fetch failed` /\n> `InvalidArgumentError: invalid content-length header`. On **TanStack Start / Nitro**\n> this fails on older Nitro (observed on `nitro@3.0.1-alpha.2`) and works on current\n> Nitro (verified on `nitro@3.0.260610-beta`) — upgrade Nitro if you hit it. Native\n> Node (and the production `node-server` build) are unaffected. OpenAI, Anthropic, and\n> fal uploads use different transports and don't exercise this path.\n\n### getFile and deleteFile\n\nProviders with a lifecycle API support `getFile()` and `deleteFile()`. Both accept the handle itself (preferred — the handle's provider type rejects a foreign provider's handle at compile time) or its raw `id`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { deleteFile, getFile, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: files,\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n\nconst meta = await getFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })\nawait deleteFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })\n```\n\n> fal storage is **upload-only** — `falFiles()` defines no `get` / `delete`, and calling `getFile()` / `deleteFile()` with it throws a clear error.\n\n### Grok (xAI): handles are public URLs\n\n`grokFiles()` uploads to the xAI Files API, then mints a [public URL](https://docs.x.ai/developers/files/public-urls) for the stored object and uses that URL as the handle's reference.\n\nxAI takes a `file_id` only on `input_file` (documents), and only on agentic-capable models. Its image path takes a URL. A public URL works for both, so one handle covers every modality on every chat model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\nimport { pngBase64 } from './image-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  // Omit `expiresAfter` for a URL that does not expire.\n  adapter: grokFiles({ expiresAfter: 86_400 }),\n  input: { data: pngBase64, mimeType: 'image/png' },\n})\n// handle.id  -> 'file_abc123'            (lifecycle)\n// handle.uri -> 'https://files-cdn.x.ai/…' (wire reference)\n```\n\nxAI limits to know:\n\n- 50 MiB per file, and PNG, JPEG, MP4, or PDF only.\n- `expiresAfter` runs from 3600 seconds (one hour) to 2592000 (thirty days).\n- Up to 1000 active public URLs per team.\n- Minting is idempotent, so re-uploading the same file returns the same URL.\n\nTo stop a URL resolving without deleting the file, call `revokePublicUrl(handle.id)` on the adapter. `deleteFile()` removes the file itself.\n\n`getFile()` mints the public URL to put it on the handle. After you revoke a URL, do not call `getFile()` for that file, or the file gets a public URL again.\n\n## Referencing a handle in a message\n\nUse `fileSourceFromHandle(handle)` to turn a `FileHandle` into a `{ type: 'file' }` content source:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { ContentPartFileSource } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst source: ContentPartFileSource = {\n  type: 'file',\n  value: 'file-abc',\n  provider: 'openai',\n}\n```\n\n- `value` is the handle exactly as the provider issued it. Treat it as opaque.\n- `provider` names the adapter that issued it.\n\nEach adapter maps `value` to its native wire field: OpenAI and Anthropic `file_id`, Gemini `fileData.fileUri`, fal storage URL, Grok public URL.\n\nA handle only works with the provider that issued it. If `provider` names a different adapter, that adapter throws a clear error. Adapters that cannot consume file handles at all are rejected before any mapping starts.\n\n### Server: upload + reference\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, fileSourceFromHandle, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicFiles, anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nexport async function askAboutPdf(pdfBase64: string, request: string) {\n  // Upload once; reuse the handle across turns.\n  const handle = await uploadFile({\n    adapter: anthropicFiles(),\n    input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n  })\n\n  return chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-5'),\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          { type: 'text', content: request },\n          { type: 'document', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Client: reuse a handle across requests\n\nUpload needs the provider key, so it happens on the server. The browser keeps the handle it gets back and puts it in the message on each turn.\n\n1. Store the handle the upload endpoint returned. Keep `{ id, provider, uri, mimeType }`.\n2. Build the source with `fileSourceFromHandle(handle)` and put it in the message content.\n3. On the server, pass the messages to `chat()` as usual.\n\nIn the browser, import `fileSourceFromHandle` from `@tanstack/ai/client`. That entry does not load server code:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { fileSourceFromHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\nimport type { FileHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\n\n// `handle` came from your upload endpoint and is stored client-side.\nfunction AskAboutFile({ handle }: { handle: FileHandle }) {\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() =>\n        sendMessage({\n          content: [\n            { type: 'text', content: 'Describe this' },\n            { type: 'image', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n          ],\n        })\n      }\n      type=\"button\"\n    >\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nOn the server, the file part arrives in the messages. Use a text adapter from the provider that issued the handle:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nexport function runTurn(messages: Array<ModelMessage>) {\n  return chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'), messages })\n}\n```\n\n> A handle from another provider throws before any request. For example, an OpenAI handle sent to a Gemini adapter fails in preflight. It is never dropped and never sent as a URL.\n\n## Provider support\n\n| Provider | Adapter | Handle referenced as | Lifecycle |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OpenAI | `openaiFiles()` | Responses `input_image` / `input_file` `file_id` | `get`, `delete` |\n| Anthropic | `anthropicFiles()` | `file_id` message source (sends the `files-api-2025-04-14` beta) | `get`, `delete` |\n| Gemini | `geminiFiles()` | `fileData.fileUri` (the handle URI) | `get`, `delete` |\n| fal | `falFiles()` | storage URL (used like any URL) | upload-only |\n| Grok (xAI) | `grokFiles()` | public URL (used like any URL) | `get`, `delete` |\n\nGemini and fal handles are URLs, so they also round-trip through a plain `{ type: 'url' }` source; OpenAI and Anthropic handles are opaque ids that require the `{ type: 'file' }` source.\n\n### Providers and endpoints that can't consume references\n\nAdapters that can consume file references declare a `supportsFileSources` capability; for everyone else (Groq, Bedrock, Mistral, OpenRouter, Ollama, BytePlus, Cohere, and any adapter written before this feature existed) `chat()` / `generateImage()` / `generateVideo()` / `embed()` reject `{ type: 'file' }` sources **before any request is built**, so a reference can never be silently mis-mapped onto a URL or data field.\n\nSome endpoints on supporting providers also have no \"reference an uploaded handle\" option — OpenAI's `images/edits` and Sora `input_reference`, and Gemini's Veo, need the actual bytes (or, for Veo, a `gs://` URI). The OpenAI **Chat Completions** image path also references images only by URL/data URI, not `file_id` — use the Responses adapter (`openaiText`) for `file_id` images. These throw a clear endpoint-specific error.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Files API\nid: files-api\ndescription: \"Upload media once and reference it by a provider-issued handle with TanStack AI's tree-shakeable files adapters (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Grok, fal).\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - files api\n  - file upload\n  - file_id\n  - fileData\n  - public url\n  - multimodal\n---\n\nProvider **Files / storage APIs** let you upload a media asset once and reference it later by a lightweight handle, instead of re-sending base64 (or relying on the provider to re-fetch a public URL) on every request. That means large or reused inputs are uploaded a single time — lower latency and bandwidth, no re-buffering of base64 on memory-constrained runtimes (e.g. Cloudflare Workers) — plus access to provider-side file lifecycle (TTL, deletion).\n\nTanStack AI exposes this as a tree-shakeable **`files` adapter** per provider, paired with a `{ type: 'file' }` [content source](./multimodal-content.md#file-handle-files-api) you drop into a message.\n\n## Files adapters\n\nEach provider with a native surface has a factory: `openaiFiles()`, `anthropicFiles()`, `geminiFiles()`, `grokFiles()`, and `falFiles()`. They read the same API-key env var as the provider's other adapters. To pass a key explicitly, use the `create*Files(apiKey)` variants (`createOpenaiFiles`, `createAnthropicFiles`, `createGeminiFiles`, `createGrokFiles`). `falFiles(config)` takes its key in the config object.\n\n```typescript\nimport { createOpenaiFiles, openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { geminiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-gemini'\nimport { anthropicFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\nimport { falFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-fal'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles() // reads OPENAI_API_KEY\nconst filesWithKey = createOpenaiFiles('sk-your-key') // explicit key\n```\n\n### uploadFile\n\nDrive an adapter with the `uploadFile()` activity function. It accepts a `Blob` (memory-efficient — preferred for large assets) or `{ data, mimeType }` where `data` is base64, and returns a `FileHandle`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: openaiFiles(),\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n// handle: { id, provider, uri?, mimeType?, sizeBytes?, expiresAt?, filename? }\n```\n\n- `id` — the provider handle used for `get` / `delete` (OpenAI/Anthropic `file_id`, Gemini file resource name, fal storage URL).\n- `uri`: the handle's URL form when the provider exposes one (Gemini file URI, fal storage URL, Grok public URL). It is `undefined` for OpenAI and Anthropic, whose handles are opaque ids.\n- `expiresAt` — epoch milliseconds, when the provider schedules the handle to expire.\n\n> **Runtime note (Gemini upload).** `geminiFiles().upload()` uses `@google/genai`'s\n> resumable upload, which sets an explicit `Content-Length` header on a `Blob`-body\n> request. Some server runtimes reject that with `fetch failed` /\n> `InvalidArgumentError: invalid content-length header`. On **TanStack Start / Nitro**\n> this fails on older Nitro (observed on `nitro@3.0.1-alpha.2`) and works on current\n> Nitro (verified on `nitro@3.0.260610-beta`) — upgrade Nitro if you hit it. Native\n> Node (and the production `node-server` build) are unaffected. OpenAI, Anthropic, and\n> fal uploads use different transports and don't exercise this path.\n\n### getFile and deleteFile\n\nProviders with a lifecycle API support `getFile()` and `deleteFile()`. Both accept the handle itself (preferred — the handle's provider type rejects a foreign provider's handle at compile time) or its raw `id`:\n\n```typescript\nimport { deleteFile, getFile, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { pdfBase64 } from './pdf-data'\n\nconst files = openaiFiles()\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  adapter: files,\n  input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n})\n\nconst meta = await getFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })\nawait deleteFile({ adapter: files, id: handle })\n```\n\n> fal storage is **upload-only** — `falFiles()` defines no `get` / `delete`, and calling `getFile()` / `deleteFile()` with it throws a clear error.\n\n### Grok (xAI): handles are public URLs\n\n`grokFiles()` uploads to the xAI Files API, then mints a [public URL](https://docs.x.ai/developers/files/public-urls) for the stored object and uses that URL as the handle's reference.\n\nxAI takes a `file_id` only on `input_file` (documents), and only on agentic-capable models. Its image path takes a URL. A public URL works for both, so one handle covers every modality on every chat model.\n\n```typescript\nimport { uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { grokFiles } from '@tanstack/ai-grok'\nimport { pngBase64 } from './image-data'\n\nconst handle = await uploadFile({\n  // Omit `expiresAfter` for a URL that does not expire.\n  adapter: grokFiles({ expiresAfter: 86_400 }),\n  input: { data: pngBase64, mimeType: 'image/png' },\n})\n// handle.id  -> 'file_abc123'            (lifecycle)\n// handle.uri -> 'https://files-cdn.x.ai/…' (wire reference)\n```\n\nxAI limits to know:\n\n- 50 MiB per file, and PNG, JPEG, MP4, or PDF only.\n- `expiresAfter` runs from 3600 seconds (one hour) to 2592000 (thirty days).\n- Up to 1000 active public URLs per team.\n- Minting is idempotent, so re-uploading the same file returns the same URL.\n\nTo stop a URL resolving without deleting the file, call `revokePublicUrl(handle.id)` on the adapter. `deleteFile()` removes the file itself.\n\n`getFile()` mints the public URL to put it on the handle. After you revoke a URL, do not call `getFile()` for that file, or the file gets a public URL again.\n\n## Referencing a handle in a message\n\nUse `fileSourceFromHandle(handle)` to turn a `FileHandle` into a `{ type: 'file' }` content source:\n\n```typescript\nimport type { ContentPartFileSource } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst source: ContentPartFileSource = {\n  type: 'file',\n  value: 'file-abc',\n  provider: 'openai',\n}\n```\n\n- `value` is the handle exactly as the provider issued it. Treat it as opaque.\n- `provider` names the adapter that issued it.\n\nEach adapter maps `value` to its native wire field: OpenAI and Anthropic `file_id`, Gemini `fileData.fileUri`, fal storage URL, Grok public URL.\n\nA handle only works with the provider that issued it. If `provider` names a different adapter, that adapter throws a clear error. Adapters that cannot consume file handles at all are rejected before any mapping starts.\n\n### Server: upload + reference\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, fileSourceFromHandle, uploadFile } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { anthropicFiles, anthropicText } from '@tanstack/ai-anthropic'\n\nexport async function askAboutPdf(pdfBase64: string, request: string) {\n  // Upload once; reuse the handle across turns.\n  const handle = await uploadFile({\n    adapter: anthropicFiles(),\n    input: { data: pdfBase64, mimeType: 'application/pdf' },\n  })\n\n  return chat({\n    adapter: anthropicText('claude-sonnet-5'),\n    messages: [\n      {\n        role: 'user',\n        content: [\n          { type: 'text', content: request },\n          { type: 'document', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n        ],\n      },\n    ],\n  })\n}\n```\n\n### Client: reuse a handle across requests\n\nUpload needs the provider key, so it happens on the server. The browser keeps the handle it gets back and puts it in the message on each turn.\n\n1. Store the handle the upload endpoint returned. Keep `{ id, provider, uri, mimeType }`.\n2. Build the source with `fileSourceFromHandle(handle)` and put it in the message content.\n3. On the server, pass the messages to `chat()` as usual.\n\nIn the browser, import `fileSourceFromHandle` from `@tanstack/ai/client`. That entry does not load server code:\n\n```tsx\nimport { useChat } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\nimport { fetchServerSentEvents } from '@tanstack/ai-client'\nimport { fileSourceFromHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\nimport type { FileHandle } from '@tanstack/ai/client'\n\n// `handle` came from your upload endpoint and is stored client-side.\nfunction AskAboutFile({ handle }: { handle: FileHandle }) {\n  const { sendMessage } = useChat({\n    connection: fetchServerSentEvents('/api/chat'),\n  })\n\n  return (\n    <button\n      onClick={() =>\n        sendMessage({\n          content: [\n            { type: 'text', content: 'Describe this' },\n            { type: 'image', source: fileSourceFromHandle(handle) },\n          ],\n        })\n      }\n      type=\"button\"\n    >\n      Ask\n    </button>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nOn the server, the file part arrives in the messages. Use a text adapter from the provider that issued the handle:\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport type { ModelMessage } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nexport function runTurn(messages: Array<ModelMessage>) {\n  return chat({ adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.6'), messages })\n}\n```\n\n> A handle from another provider throws before any request. For example, an OpenAI handle sent to a Gemini adapter fails in preflight. It is never dropped and never sent as a URL.\n\n## Provider support\n\n| Provider | Adapter | Handle referenced as | Lifecycle |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| OpenAI | `openaiFiles()` | Responses `input_image` / `input_file` `file_id` | `get`, `delete` |\n| Anthropic | `anthropicFiles()` | `file_id` message source (sends the `files-api-2025-04-14` beta) | `get`, `delete` |\n| Gemini | `geminiFiles()` | `fileData.fileUri` (the handle URI) | `get`, `delete` |\n| fal | `falFiles()` | storage URL (used like any URL) | upload-only |\n| Grok (xAI) | `grokFiles()` | public URL (used like any URL) | `get`, `delete` |\n\nGemini and fal handles are URLs, so they also round-trip through a plain `{ type: 'url' }` source; OpenAI and Anthropic handles are opaque ids that require the `{ type: 'file' }` source.\n\n### Providers and endpoints that can't consume references\n\nAdapters that can consume file references declare a `supportsFileSources` capability; for everyone else (Groq, Bedrock, Mistral, OpenRouter, Ollama, BytePlus, Cohere, and any adapter written before this feature existed) `chat()` / `generateImage()` / `generateVideo()` / `embed()` reject `{ type: 'file' }` sources **before any request is built**, so a reference can never be silently mis-mapped onto a URL or data field.\n\nSome endpoints on supporting providers also have no \"reference an uploaded handle\" option — OpenAI's `images/edits` and Sora `input_reference`, and Gemini's Veo, need the actual bytes (or, for Veo, a `gs://` URI). The OpenAI **Chat Completions** image path also references images only by URL/data URI, not `file_id` — use the Responses adapter (`openaiText`) for `file_id` images. These throw a clear endpoint-specific error.\n"}
